/* Notable — English.

   The keys are the German source strings: Notable was written in German, and the
   German text in the code IS the key. This file is what turns it into English. A
   key that is missing here falls back to itself, which means German shows through
   in an English window — so a gap is visible rather than silent, and
   LocalizationTests fails on one.

   Two things are deliberate and look like mistakes:

   - Entries that map to themselves. Numbers, separators, key names and product
     names must not be translated.
   - Some sentences appear twice, once with %@ and once with %lld. The key of an
     interpolated string carries the specifier of the interpolated *type*, and Int
     produces %lld where String produces %@. Both spellings are kept so a lookup
     cannot miss on the wrong one. */

